@page "/auth/tos"
@model Roblox.Website.Pages.Auth.Privacy

@{
    Layout = "Shared/_Layout";
}

@section MetaTags {
    <title>Terms of Service</title>
}

<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 offset-lg-3">
            <h2 class="mt-4 mb-4">Terms of Service</h2>
            <p>Last Updated August 11, 2026</p>
            <p>This is essentially just a list of rules for our platform. We reserve the right to update this at any time without any notice, so check here frequently in case the terms are updated. For privacy information, <a href="/auth/privacy">click here</a>.</p>
            <p>A violation of any of these rules could result in a temporary OR permanent ban. New accounts will usually be permanently banned on their first infraction, while older accounts might be given temporary bans (e.g. 1 day or 1 week) depending on the severity.</p>
            <p class="mb-0 fw-bolder">Text Guidelines</p>
            <p>These apply to all text inputs on the site, such as forum posts and in-game chat.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not discriminate or harass people.</span> Light swearing is OK, but don't use slurs as an insult.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not reveal personal information pertaining to yourself or others.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Try not to start drama.</span> For example, do not create posts "exposing" someone. If you are concerned about a user, you should send a message to a moderator.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not excessively advertise websites, YouTube channels, Twitter accounts, or other off-platform URLs.</span> You can mention stuff like "Hey, I own example.com", but if you start spamming "join my site" or "subscribe to my YouTube channel", you're going to be banned.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-4 mb-0 fw-bolder">Image Guidelines</p>
            <p>As well as the above text guidelines, these guidelines apply to images uploaded to the site:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not upload violent content.</span> Examples include gore, violent scenes from movies, etc.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not upload content with real people.</span> Exceptions will be made for celebrities if it's obvious who they are.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not upload pornographic content featuring underage characters.</span> Even if the character is officially a 500 year old vampire, if it looks underage, you shouldn't upload it.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-4 mb-0 fw-bolder">Other Notes</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">You are responsible for invited users.</span> For example, if you invite someone who starts spamming racial slurs on the forums, your account could get banned. You should only invite people you trust.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">You are responsible for the security of your account.</span> Password resets are done on a case-by-case basis, depending on if you can verify that you actually owned the account. Pick a strong password - if you forget it or someone guesses it, you may permanently lose access to your account.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">A few alternate accounts is OK.</span> You can create an alt by creating an invite and joining using the invite URL. Do not create alt accounts with the application system.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="fw-bolder">Do not use the advertising system for advertising URLs that are not relevant to this website.</span> For example, discord servers pertaining to this website (or old Roblox in general) would be ok. A URL pointing to an unknown website (such as "my-revival.com"), your YouTube channel, your Twitch channel, etc, would not be allowed.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="mt-4 mb-4">xnr's "Fair Market" Law</h2>
            <p>Act No. 001 -- Status: Active</p>
            <p>This law ensures that the economy will be stable for as long as possible, while also protecting against abuse of administrative powers. e.g. spawning in assets, creating artificial robux for personal or third party use.</p>
            
            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">I. Controlled Economy</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Monetary Control</span> - No position, whether above, below, or within economy may create, grant, transfer, duplicate, or otherwise distribute any form of currency to themselves or another person without authorization from the Economy Department, as uncontrolled currency creation can cause hyperinflation, market distortion, wealth dilution, and potentially the collapse of the economy.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Asset Control</span> - No position, whether above, below, or within economy may create, grant, transfer, duplicate, or otherwise distribute any accessory, limited, or off-sale item/s, to themselves or another person without authorization from the Economy Department, as unrestricted asset creation can destroy scarcity, artificially create wealth, and create hidden wealth.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Anti-Manipulation</span> - No position may use administrative powers, alternate accounts, intermediaries, trades, or other methods to bypass these restrictions or manipulate currency, item supply, prices, or trades for personal or third-party benefit.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">II. Economic Oversight</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Distribution Oversight</span> - ALL authorized currency or accessory distributions must be approved by Economy and recorded with the recipient, amount/item, reason, and date.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Audit & Transparency</span> - ALL economic transactions, creations, and distributions must be permanently logged and made available for review by authorized oversight personnel.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Conflict of Interest</span> - No Economy member may approve, authorize, or oversee a transaction that directly benefits themselves, their alternate accounts, or individuals acting on their behalf.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">III. Enforcement</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Violation Procedures</span> - Any suspected violation must be investigated and documented before disciplinary action is taken, unless immediate action is necessary to prevent further economic damage.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Penalties</span> - Anyone found violating the Fair Market Law may have their economic privileges revoked and may face demotion, suspension, removal, or other disciplinary action depending on the severity of the violation.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Restitution</span> - Any currency or assets obtained through an unauthorized creation, distribution, transfer, or manipulation may be removed or reversed where technically possible.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">IV. Administrative Protection</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Equal Application</span> - These laws apply to every position regardless of rank, including Owners, Co-owners, Economy staff, and other administrators.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Authority Limitation</span> - No position may override or bypass these laws solely because of its rank or administrative authority.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Anti-Retaliation</span> - No person may punish, demote, or otherwise retaliate against someone for legitimately reporting a suspected violation of the Fair Market Law.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="mt-4 mb-4">xnr's "Smooth Circulation" Act</h2>
            <p>Act No. 002 -- Status: Active </p>
            <p>This act ensures that the flow of currency and trading of limiteds is smooth and stable for as long as possible, and keeping it away from problems such as: price manipulation, overhoarding, and artificial scarcity.</p>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">I. Robux Circulation</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Circulation Preservation</span> - No position, whether above, below, or within the economy may intentionally remove, hoard, lock, or otherwise restrict a substantial amount of Robux from active circulation for the purpose of creating artificial scarcity, inflating prices, or manipulating the economy.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Liquidity Protection</span> - Robux must remain reasonably available for legitimate transactions, trading, and economic activity. No person may intentionally concentrate excessive amounts of Robux among themselves, their alternate accounts, or associated individuals for the purpose of restricting market liquidity.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Artificial Scarcity</span> - No position may intentionally create or maintain an artificial shortage of Robux through coordinated hoarding, withholding, restricted trading, or other methods for personal or third-party benefit.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Anti-Manipulation</span> - No position may use administrative powers, alternate accounts, intermediaries, trades, or other methods to bypass these restrictions or manipulate Robux circulation, supply, prices, or transactions for personal or third party benefit.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">II. Economic Oversight</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Circulation Monitoring</span> - The Economy Department shall monitor the total estimated Robux in circulation and identify significant changes in supply, distribution, concentration, and transaction activity.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Economic Intervention</span> - If Robux circulation falls to an unsafe level, the Economy Department may authorize measures to restore liquidity, including authorized stipends, rewards, grants, events, or other controlled distributions.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Distribution Oversight</span> - All authorized Robux injections or distributions must be approved by Economy and recorded with the recipient, amount, reason, and date.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Audit & Transparency</span> - All authorized Robux creations, distributions, and significant economic interventions must be permanently logged and made available for review by authorized oversight personnel.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">III. Market Stability</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Price Manipulation</span> - No person may deliberately restrict Robux supply for the purpose of forcing buyers to pay unreasonable or artificially inflated prices.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Hoarding Threshold</span> - Holding Robux for legitimate savings, investment, or ordinary trading is permitted. Possessing a large balance alone shall not constitute a violation unless there is evidence of intentional economic manipulation.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Controlled Issuance</span> - The Economy Department shall avoid unnecessary Robux issuance when circulation is already sufficient, as excessive issuance may cause inflation, currency dilution, and loss of purchasing power.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Circulation Target</span> - The Economy Department shall maintain a healthy level of Robux circulation and may establish or revise circulation targets based on the number of active accounts, daily stipends, transaction volume, and overall economic conditions.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">IV. Enforcement</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Violation Procedures</span> - Any suspected violation must be investigated and documented before disciplinary action is taken, unless immediate action is necessary to prevent further economic damage.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Penalties</span> - Anyone found violating the Robux Circulation law may have their economic privileges revoked and may face demotion, suspension, removal, or other disciplinary action depending on the severity of the violation.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Restitution</span> - Any Robux obtained or withheld through unauthorized creation, distribution, hoarding, or manipulation may be removed, redistributed, or reversed where technically possible.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bolder mt-3">V. Administrative Protection</h5>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Equal Application</span> - These laws apply to every position regardless of rank, including Owners, Co-owners, Economy staff, and other administrators.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Authority Limitation</span> - No position may override or bypass these laws solely because of its rank or administrative authority.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Anti-Retaliation</span> - No person may punish, demote, or otherwise retaliate against someone for legitimately reporting a suspected violation of the Robux Circulation Law.</li>
                <li><span class="fw-bolder">Economic Neutrality</span> - The Economy Department must act to preserve the stability and liquidity of the Robux economy rather than favoring individual holders, sellers, buyers, or groups.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>